[{"id":68814,"sender_id":639,"sender_full_name":"Praphulla Koushik","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4d3ba0c0a767b7329e0f56993aceb259?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/bibundles.20composition/near/68814\">#1</a> I would like to ask question about https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/bibundle#composition</p>\n<p>I have asked a question here https://mathoverflow.net/questions/303781/composition-of-bibundles asking for motivation why would one want to define composition as <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><msub><mo>×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(E\\times_{\\mathcal{H}_0}F)/H</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0001em;vertical-align:-0.2501em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\"><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathcal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0097em;\">H</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3173em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.357em;margin-left:-0.0097em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.143em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2501em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span></span></span></span> and not just <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><msub><mo>×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E\\times_{\\mathcal{H}_0}F</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9334em;vertical-align:-0.2501em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\"><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathcal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0097em;\">H</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3173em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.357em;margin-left:-0.0097em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.143em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2501em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span></span></span></span>. Is that just a choice? I guess it is not. </p>\n<p>https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0702399.pdf says in page 6 says that <strong>Viewing a bibundle as relation of stacks suggests defining the composition of bibundles as <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><msub><mo>×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(E\\times_{\\mathcal{H}_0}F)/H</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0001em;vertical-align:-0.2501em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\"><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathcal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0097em;\">H</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3173em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.357em;margin-left:-0.0097em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.143em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2501em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span></span></span></span></strong></p>\n<p>I believe a little more details about what is that motivation of viewing bibundle as relation of stacks in https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/bibundle#composition  would be  useful.</p>\n<p>Apologies if this discussion is not suitable here.</p>","timestamp":1530363047,"subject":"bibundles composition","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68818,"sender_id":43,"sender_full_name":"DavidRoberts","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fbc2dbfb28f9e9275a4fd4cd109b5a21?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/bibundles.20composition/near/68818\">#2</a> The short answer is that the naive operation <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><msub><mo>×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E\\times_{\\mathcal{H}_0}F</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9334em;vertical-align:-0.2501em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\"><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathcal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0097em;\">H</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3173em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.357em;margin-left:-0.0097em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.143em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2501em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span></span></span></span> does not result in a bibundle. I will provide more details at the MO question before too long.</p>\n<p>[Also: to get the maths to render, you can edit your post and select the “Markdown+Itex” option below the text box.]</p>","timestamp":1530405059,"subject":"bibundles composition","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68824,"sender_id":639,"sender_full_name":"Praphulla Koushik","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4d3ba0c0a767b7329e0f56993aceb259?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/bibundles.20composition/near/68824\">#3</a> Thank you @DavidRoberts. </p>\n<p>I am not even able to see what could go wrong for <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><msub><mo>×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E\\times_{\\mathcal{H}_0}F</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9334em;vertical-align:-0.2501em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\"><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathcal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0097em;\">H</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3173em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.357em;margin-left:-0.0097em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.143em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2501em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span></span></span></span> to be a bibundle. May be I am ignoring something important.</p>","timestamp":1530452220,"subject":"bibundles composition","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68830,"sender_id":237,"sender_full_name":"Richard Williamson","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b90dbe6063b47a44f7308efebb6ade2b?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/bibundles.20composition/near/68830\">#4</a> Just to say thanks for asking your question here, Praphulla, it is very welcome and suitable.</p>","timestamp":1530549691,"subject":"bibundles composition","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68848,"sender_id":639,"sender_full_name":"Praphulla Koushik","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4d3ba0c0a767b7329e0f56993aceb259?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/bibundles.20composition/near/68848\">#5</a> Thank you @Richard Williamson:)</p>\n<p>Can I know who has written that part so that I can ping that author.</p>","timestamp":1530621950,"subject":"bibundles composition","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68850,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/bibundles.20composition/near/68850\">#6</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Can I know who has written that part so that I can ping that author.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>There is a button “history” at the bottom of each <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span>Lab page, which takes you to the edit history. </p>\n<p>Looking through it, the section “Composition” was added in <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/bibundle/24\">rev 24</a> by Chenchang Zhu.</p>","timestamp":1530624515,"subject":"bibundles composition","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68851,"sender_id":29,"sender_full_name":"Todd_Trimble","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/078428beaeaddf058781b9be6b2c240f?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/bibundles.20composition/near/68851\">#7</a> There is no ‘pinging’ mechanism here that I am aware of (like the @ used at MO). </p>\n<p>Maybe it should also be added that Chenchang is not a regular nLab user and so very likely would be unaware that you want her attention, unless you email her directly.</p>","timestamp":1530625287,"subject":"bibundles composition","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68867,"sender_id":639,"sender_full_name":"Praphulla Koushik","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4d3ba0c0a767b7329e0f56993aceb259?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/bibundles.20composition/near/68867\">#8</a> Thank you Todd Trimble and Urs.</p>\n<p>I will email Chenchang Zhu. :) Thank you.</p>","timestamp":1530668606,"subject":"bibundles composition","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68869,"sender_id":43,"sender_full_name":"DavidRoberts","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fbc2dbfb28f9e9275a4fd4cd109b5a21?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/bibundles.20composition/near/68869\">#9</a> For what it’s worth, I have written something over at <a href=\"https://mathoverflow.net/questions/303781/composition-of-bibundles/304203#304203\">MathOverflow</a>.</p>","timestamp":1530680221,"subject":"bibundles composition","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":68889,"sender_id":639,"sender_full_name":"Praphulla Koushik","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4d3ba0c0a767b7329e0f56993aceb259?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/bibundles.20composition/near/68889\">#10</a> I saw those answers. Thank you :)</p>","timestamp":1530706939,"subject":"bibundles composition","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]}]